### 6\. Custom symbolic notation

The original sequence is retained:

`·—>^✓-<=|''',.\_`

Its components receive the following assigned functions.

| Symbol | Class | Assigned function | |---|---|---| | `·` | Reference | Identifies a point or subject | | `—>` | Transition | Connects an initial state to a destination | | `^` | Modifier | Qualifies the following token | | `✓` | Validation | Indicates that a defined check passed | | `-` | Relation | Distinguishes or separates values | | `<=` | Comparison | Less than or equal to | | `|` | Boundary | Separates fields | | `'''` | Literal delimiter | Identifies a designated text field | | `,` | Separator | Separates elements | | `.` | Terminator | Closes a statement | | `\` | Escape | Controls interpretation of a following character | | `_` | Identifier | Represents a named field or identifier |

### Combination rules

R1 — Token recognition: Read each symbol individually before interpreting a combination.

R2 — Modifier binding: `^` applies to the next eligible token.

R3 — Directional binding: `—>` indicates a declared transition.

R4 — Comparison binding: `<=` requires a left operand and a right operand.

R5 — Boundary binding: `|` separates fields.

R6 — Literal handling: Apostrophes and punctuation retain their literal meaning unless a declared grammar assigns another function.

R7 — Escape handling: `\` must identify which following character it controls.

R8 — Verification: `✓` indicates a passed check only when the verification procedure and supporting evidence are defined.

